comments[8]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-05T16:12:56.489Z","harness:codex","Implementation choice: use maintained Markdown lexer and GitHub-compatible slugger in the development-only docs gate. Official heading rules checked at https://docs.github.com/en/get-started/writing-on-github/getting-started-with-writing-and-formatting-on-github/basic-writing-and-formatting-syntax. Tests will cover fenced examples, inline formatting, duplicate headings, Unicode, local fragments and transitive reachability."
  "2026-09-05T16:54:18.331Z","harness:codex","Negative-control discovery: a heading containing HTML entities currently generates cats-amp-dogs instead of the rendered GitHub anchor cats--dogs. Added a regression before correcting entity decoding. Documentation parsing remains a development gate only, with no production import or runtime cost."
  "2026-09-05T16:59:43.852Z","harness:codex","Quality tooling: adopted compatible ESLint 10.10.0 and development-only marked/github-slugger/entities for rendered Markdown navigation checks. Negative controls cover encoded URLs, disconnected cycles, stale or empty exemptions, duplicate headings, nested formatting, HTML entities, code spans, images, and custom anchors. No gate bypass or coverage exclusion added."
  "2026-09-05T17:10:30.082Z","harness:codex","Acceptance scope check: recovered the July source revision to identify the four paragraphs despite line drift. Restructured package scaffold/loading, garbage collection, and automatic-fix scope prose into actionable bullets; kept EXTENSIONS.md within the unchanged 450-line gate. Updated command-reference file-report semantics and remote reference normalization. Full docs-and-skills gate passes."
  "2026-09-05T17:53:06.729Z","harness:codex","Final local evidence: 8457 tests across 617 files pass at exact 100% lines/statements/functions/branches (60094/62503/12956/47351 covered). Full quality:static passes, including unchanged token ceilings, docstrings, graph composition, and record integrity. Typecheck, version policy, ShellCheck, credential scan, zero-vulnerability dependency audit, and enforced Trivy scan pass. Final npm/npx and Bun/bunx packed smoke covers all 13 packages; separate temporary installed SDK/CLI acceptance passes. Required Sentry/telemetry gate passes with zero blocking Sentry groups and no failures lacking error codes. PR review and hosted checks are the remaining delivery stage."
  "2026-09-05T18:11:35.041Z","harness:codex","Review recurrence: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/pull/1204 identifies image-only reachability, unquoted HTML anchors, and test fixture fallback. CodeQL alert 38 flags regex HTML stripping in heading extraction; no executable HTML sink exists, but a maintained HTML parser will remove the fragile step. Add negative controls before implementation; retain existing coverage and gate thresholds."
  "2026-09-05T18:18:54.543Z","harness:codex","PR #1204 review: replaced regex HTML stripping with parse5 8.0.1. Negative controls prove correct heading text when quoted attributes contain >, recognize quoted/unquoted id/name attributes, ignore comment pseudo-anchors, and preserve encoded inline-code semantics. CodeQL alert 38 had no executable HTML sink, and the flagged pattern is removed instead of suppressing analysis. Moved/added declaration docstrings for touched helpers without weakening any documentation gate."
  "2026-09-05T18:34:25.247Z","harness:codex","PR #1204 round-one dispositions recorded on every original review/comment surface with up/down reactions. Three documentation/test findings fixed; two unsupported findings answered with source and tracker evidence. Regex heading stripping removed after CodeQL alert 38; hosted revalidation remains pending on the next head. Final local proof: 8458 tests in 617 files, exact coverage 60107/60107 lines, 62520/62520 statements, 12957/12957 functions, 47365/47365 branches. All 68 touched named non-test functions have declaration JSDoc. Full static/type/documentation gates, all five PM-linked runs, final npm/npx+Bun/bunx 13-package smoke, separate temporary packed acceptance, dependency audit, and immutable tracked-tree Trivy scan pass. Sourcery substantive review is unavailable under its current quota; Greptile has not responded. These are availability limitations, not approval."
